<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  launchd agent for the card recon mailbox poller (Mac mini).

  Deliberately the SAME mechanism as com.marathon.socialpublish and
  com.marathon.shopifyreconcile: a user LaunchAgent in ~/Library/LaunchAgents
  running node against the repo checkout, with its logs under the repo, and
  single-flight enforced by scripts/lib/launchdRunner.mjs. No second scheduling
  system is introduced, and nothing here is a new idea.

  Differences from the social publisher, and why:

    · RunAtLoad is TRUE. The publisher's is false because loading the agent —
      after a reboot, or while installing it — must not fire a post to a live
      Instagram account. Nothing this job does is irreversible: it reads a
      mailbox and submits what it finds to a capture path that refuses
      duplicates. Firing on load means the mailbox is checked the moment the
      agent loads rather than up to five minutes later.

      BE PRECISE ABOUT WHAT "RESTARTS WITH THE MACHINE" MEANS HERE. This is a
      user LaunchAgent, and a user LaunchAgent loads when that user's GUI
      session begins — at LOGIN, not at boot. It survives a restart of this
      machine because the machine logs itself in: `autoLoginUser =
      marathonclub` (verified 2026-08-29), which is also the only reason the
      other two com.marathon agents work the way everyone assumes they do.
      Turn auto-login off, or leave the mini sitting at a login window after a
      power cut, and NONE of the three run — the mailbox simply stops being
      checked, and the Card recon tab's heartbeat is what says so.

      A LaunchDaemon would not have that dependency, and is deliberately not
      used: a daemon runs as root outside any user session, which is a
      different security posture, a different credential story (the
      service-account key and the .env both live in this user's home) and a
      second scheduling pattern on a machine that has one. (CodeRabbit, PR #510.)

    · StartInterval 300, not 120. A batch report is emailed once a day per
      terminal at settlement. Five minutes is already far faster than anyone
      needs and is a twelfth of the IMAP connections a two-minute tick would
      make. A tick with no unread mail exits in under a second.

    · A MISSED FIRE is run by launchd as soon as the machine wakes, which is
      the behaviour we want: a slip that arrived while the mini was off is
      captured late rather than never.

  NODE PATH: /opt/homebrew/bin/node — this is an Apple-silicon Mac mini, where
  Homebrew installs under /opt/homebrew, and launchd resolves
  ProgramArguments[0] itself without consulting PATH. The installer rewrites
  this line to whichever node it actually finds and refuses to install if that
  binary is missing, so the two cannot drift apart.

  CREDENTIALS: nothing secret belongs in this file — it is committed. The
  mailbox user and its Gmail APP PASSWORD live in the gitignored .env at the
  repo root, read at run time. Only PATHS appear here, never values.
  GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS is the same service-account key the other two
  agents already point at; it is what lets the poller mint its own identity's
  token and write /card_batch_intake.

  INSTALL: scripts/cardrecon/install-card-recon-poller.sh. Paths below assume
  the checkout at /Users/marathonclub/marathon-store-app — change BOTH the
  ProgramArguments path and WorkingDirectory if it lives elsewhere.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.marathon.cardreconpoll</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/node</string>
    <string>/Users/marathonclub/marathon-store-app/scripts/cardrecon/poll-runner.mjs</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/marathonclub/marathon-store-app</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS</key><string>/Users/marathonclub/.config/marathon/shopify-reconciler-sa.json</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>300</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <!-- launchd's own capture is the LAST-RESORT log: anything the runner could
       not handle itself (node failing to start, a syntax error) lands here.
       The readable per-run log is logs/card-recon-poll.log, written and
       rotated by the runner. -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/marathonclub/marathon-store-app/logs/card-recon-launchd.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/marathonclub/marathon-store-app/logs/card-recon-launchd.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
